\description{
Samples a brain volume at the positions of the cortical surface vertices of a subject and returns the resulting per-vertex values. This is the equivalent of the FreeSurfer command line tool \code{mri_vol2surf} (or of the \code{project_vol2surf} function of the Python package \code{yabplot}), implemented in R. The volume and the surface must be defined in the same coordinate space, which is the case for the volumes in the \code{mri} directory of a subject (e.g., \code{brain.mgz}) and the surfaces in its \code{surf} directory (e.g., \code{lh.white}) -- both are in the subject's native space.

